{"step_index":748,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T23:09:30Z","input_tokens":3001,"cache_read_tokens":204687,"output_tokens":865,"thinking":"The error indicates a permission issue, specifically a denial of deletion. This points directly to the Firestore security rules. Examination of the rules confirms that deletions are explicitly disallowed for submissions within quizzes. Therefore, the \"Clear Students\" function's inability to delete is expected.\n\n\nThe Firestore rule restricting deletions directly causes the \"Clear Students\" function's failure. Allowing deletion in the `submissions` rule is required for this function to work, updating the rule to permit `delete` or allowing `write` for `submissions` under a quiz.\n\nThe modal confirmation for the clear students action requires specific text and buttons. The modal must display the text \"Are you sure this is what you want?\" with \"Yes\" and \"No\" buttons, closing on \"No\" and triggering the Firestore clear on \"Yes.\" Auto submissions should default to off, reflected in `teacher.html`, Firestore, and the student interface, with appropriate UI indications. Non-major Patch 1.0.17 requires an update entry in `HISTORY.md`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"firestore batch delete collection web javascript compat\""}}]}
{"step_index":749,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T23:09:41Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-09T07:09:41+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-09T07:09:45+08:00\nThe search for \"firestore batch delete collection web javascript compat\" returned the following summary:\nTo delete an entire Cloud Firestore collection using the **Web Namespaced / Compat API (Version 8 syntax)**, you cannot delete the collection directly with a single command[1]. Instead, you must fetch documents in batches and use write batches (`db.batch()`) to delete them iteratively (since Firestore batches are limited to a maximum of 500 writes at a time)[2][3].\n\nHere is a robust helper function using the **v8 compat syntax** (`firebase.firestore()`)[2]:\n\n```javascript\n/**\n * Deletes a Firestore collection in batches using the Web v8 compat syntax.\n * \n * @param {firebase.firestore.Firestore} db - The Firestore compat instance\n * @param {string} collectionPath - The path to the collection (e.g., 'users/123/orders')\n * @param {number} batchSize - Number of documents to delete per batch (max 500)\n */\nasync function deleteCollection(db, collectionPath, batchSize) {\n  const collectionRef = db.collection(collectionPath);\n  const query = collectionRef.orderBy('__name__').limit(batchSize);\n\n  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n    deleteQueryBatch(db, query, batchSize, resolve, reject);\n  });\n}\n\nasync function deleteQueryBatch(db, query, batchSize, resolve, reject) {\n  try {\n    const snapshot = await query.get();\n\n    // If there are no documents left, we are done\n    if (snapshot.size === 0) {\n      resolve();\n      return;\n    }\n\n    // Otherwise, delete documents in a batch\n    const batch = db.batch();\n    snapshot.docs.forEach((doc) => {\n      batch.delete(doc.ref);\n    });\n\n    await batch.commit();\n\n    // Recurse on the next batch to avoid memory issues and handle large collections\n    process.nextTick\n    setTimeout(() => {\n      deleteQueryBatch(db, query, batchSize, resolve, reject);\n    }, 0);\n\n  } catch (error) {\n    reject(error);\n  }\n}\n\n// --- How to call it ---\n// const db = firebase.firestore();\n// deleteCollecti\n<truncated 594 bytes>\nions, it is strongly recommended to run deletion scripts via a trusted environment (like Node.js with `firebase-admin`)[3] or use the Firebase CLI command (`firebase firestore:delete`)[6].\n\nSources:\n[1] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEJQZirxiOCqxgDKJuRMVW2RE9gdyl2ev_j-k8hIr0D-vuKxCMMtnfF92dL6JGO9UjSP9NIGk09OqsZRIDsIuAXKHyb7ki2YtqqQD98JNjee18uRXpn-VF067RV0CEr627GEs1glMf5rrZuUMy_7A7stpLl4l2RhCpxxTYuybPU3EazkYhgDHsTGORhhVC0tvSOu1z1C94iOw==)\n[2] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFeq39kxJbkWgHM3df3EH2YRkXLWQGZNwQwSGg2Tza9cbRg_p4fLvb3kmDqyuM2mdzJ6t87UCTIox_6YpBE6G5mw5nCiHifRcPC1tTVBAxyufQr4mnrvzxtw0o_E4HHQNMHDNe-zfqIURhLXWh_I37dk70XPlAuL5s1XZwLv7BILgBpZ3GQlr4xoZXohrtHI6Ve)\n[3] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGmIw58O-jBoW_6fU_YAfEnzjsSCi0L95C3SgpUaCAUAR2eDD8LjEsXbju2s1MVt3SRJAyfxfnXQ4RzyamltJyuPk605YFd8ap5hsIpgJRP3dD1P44SodklUDjGhSM0UAwrKXdYCpclEIP_EpTcrD-KpxSddkbcGkqy7UpBDEIQiiviWxNwQ5YvmnMh7hw5yya9Cg==)\n[4] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHmIF_F7T6ktMpKmBcZfdgIw7Gd6afhuUrzNnnqPfsYEI6f6wmWKV_l0fDsf0lsMZjbE2Tm_Tf1B9QM9ixScnmccHu5E3CfuvUUhH931TcC3wbEIPsT9MI2bACgMLfheO6a7GDny09Wge02Ql_Uv-IHZodne5TPGpK6SHDfTUY1g724tX1pl2xNgPxCA1erKO57mMgb6x9b3u6D1MxI0Z-beVg0Z6tti4RUWa7zhvMIhsf3SA==)\n[5] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGmEGPI5i1oM9Ad1cUUUvmz4eBJT2H01nAEHggnzklIeiWrnZ9ph7WKw8yim-Ib2gmrkDkWadBHB7LEi6GTvsJ9eOv-YUHjcyvnLOdbscX3tCa8S97zbqrpAt-wTL5Ef2lRXW0fS7B2CK0OeDjJx7X5WZE28Jr8a_VflCRzgR0XFwk=)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFeq39kxJbkWgHM3df3EH2YRkXLWQGZNwQwSGg2Tza9cbRg_p4fLvb3kmDqyuM2mdzJ6t87UCTIox_6YpBE6G5mw5nCiHifRcPC1tTVBAxyufQr4mnrvzxtw0o_E4HHQNMHDNe-zfqIURhLXWh_I37dk70XPlAuL5s1XZwLv7BILgBpZ3GQlr4xoZXohrtHI6Ve)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
